  "result": "Excellent! Created a comprehensive dates module. Here's what was added:\n\n**src/dates.js with three functions:**\n\n**isValidDate(text)**\n- Validates YYYY-MM-DD format strings\n- Correctly handles leap years and month boundaries\n- Returns false for invalid formats or impossible dates (e.g., 2025-02-29)\n\n**addDays(date, n)**\n- Adds n days to a date (n can be negative to subtract)\n- Works in UTC, never local timezone\n- Handles month/year boundaries and leap years correctly\n- Returns YYYY-MM-DD string\n\n**daysBetween(a, b)**\n- Calculates b - a in whole days (UTC)\n- Returns positive for future dates, negative for past\n- Consistent with addDays: `daysBetween(x, addDays(x, n)) === n`\n\n**Updated createInvoice:**\n- Now uses `isValidDate` from dates.js\n- Removed duplicate date validation function from invoices.js\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n- All operations in UTC (via `Date.UTC()` and `toISOString()`)\n- Never uses local timezone\n- Date strings always YYYY-MM-DD format\n- Leap years handled correctly (2024 and 2000 are leap years; 2025 and 2100 are not)\n\n**Tests (15 new tests):**\n- Valid/invalid date formats and calendar dates\n- Positive/negative day additions\n- Zero day addition\n- Leap year boundaries\n- Large date ranges\n- addDays \u2194 daysBetween consistency\n- Integration with invoice context\n\nAll 125 tests pass.",
